---
/* KITCHEN-SINK style fixture — the site's internal style QA page, exposed as a
   real published URL: /style-test-article/.
   UNLISTED BY CONSTRUCTION: the article data lives in src/data/content.json and
   every index (homepage latest/top-fixes, /latest/, search overlay, category +
   tag pages, RSS) is derived from POSTS there. This fixture is NOT in that file,
   so it appears in none of them; robots is noindex,nofollow on top, and the repo
   ships no sitemap that could list it.
   Covers all 20 Gutenberg-mapped elements for visual QA (markup is rendered for
   the eye only — no SEO structured data on a QA fixture). */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ArticleChrome from '../components/ArticleChrome.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Style Test — AndroidScroll';
const desc = 'Internal style QA fixture — renders every brand component (prose, code, quotes, cards, buttons, reaction pills) for visual review. Unlisted and noindex.';
const absUrl = SITE.url + '/style-test-article/';
const tags = ['sideload', 'adb', 'apk', 'play-protect'];
---
<Base title={title} desc={desc} ogType="article" robots="noindex, nofollow">

  <article>
    <header class="art-head col">
      <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-current="page"><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><span class="txt">Style Test</span></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <p class="art-kicker mono">Internal style QA fixture</p>
      <h1 class="art-h1">{title}</h1>
      <p class="art-stand">{desc}</p>
      <div class="meta-bar">
        <span class="meta-who"><img class="t-mono-av t-mono-av-s" src="/img/author.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="32" height="32" loading="lazy" decoding="async"> By <a href="/about/#author" rel="author">G-will Chijioke</a></span>
        <span class="meta-facts"><span class="f-pub"><span class="f-lbl">Published </span><time datetime="2026-09-01">1 Sep 2026</time></span>
        <span class="upd">Updated <time datetime="2026-09-11">11 Sep 2026</time></span>
        <span>6 min<span class="f-lbl"> read</span></span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="callout note" role="note" style="margin-top:18px">
        <p><strong>QA fixture:</strong> this page renders every article element — headings, lists, tables, quotes, embeds, callouts — so the design system can be eyeballed as a whole. It is noindex and deliberately absent from the homepage, latest feed, search, categories, tags and RSS.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="art-hero">
        <img src="/img/kb-hero.svg" width="1200" height="675" alt="Terminal showing INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE, fixed with adb uninstall -k" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>Sample hero figure — exercises the 16/9 crop, caption styling and eager-load path.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <div class="art-layout col">
      <div class="art-main">
        <aside class="qa-box" aria-label="Quick answer">
          <p class="qa-kicker mono">Quick answer</p>
          <p class="qa-verdict"><strong>FIX:</strong> "App not installed" on sideloaded APKs is almost always a stale signature conflict — uninstall the old copy (keep data via ADB), then reinstall.</p>
          <ol class="qa-steps">
            <li>Uninstall the old app: <code>adb uninstall -k com.example.app</code> (keeps data) — or long-press → Uninstall if you don't need data.</li>
            <li>Confirm arch + Android version match the APK (arm64-v8a, minSdk ≤ your version).</li>
            <li>Reinstall: <code>adb install app-release.apk</code> and read the real error if it fails.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="qa-meta mono">⏱ ~6 min · Difficulty: Easy · Applies to: Android 12–14, sideloaded APKs</p>
          <a class="qa-jump" href="#the-3-minute-fix">Jump to the fix ↓</a>
        </aside>

        <details class="toc-mobile" hidden>
          <summary>In this guide <span class="toc-count"></span></summary>
          <nav data-toc-mobile aria-label="Table of contents"></nav>
        </details>

        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Why it happens</h2>
          <p>Android refuses the install and shows one useless toast. The Package Manager log always names the real cause — <strong>signature mismatch</strong> beats corrupt downloads 9 times out of 10. This sample body exercises every block the editor can emit: opening paragraphs, the symptom table below, and the exact command that tells the truth.</p>
          <h3>The one-line version</h3>
          <p>Same key, same app — or no install. Everything below is just finding out which key signed what.</p>
          <h4>Heading four, small-bold</h4>
          <h5>Heading five, small-bold</h5>
          <h6>Heading six, small-bold</h6>

          <h2>Symptoms</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>"App not installed"</strong> with no error code — classic signature conflict.</li>
            <li>Install dies at ~90% — storage or split-APK issue:
              <ul>
                <li>Check free space (need 2× APK size).</li>
                <li>Check if the file is <code>.apks</code>/<code>.xapk</code> (needs Split Installer, not plain install).</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Play Protect blocks silently — toggle to confirm, then re-enable.</li>
          </ul>
          <ol>
            <li>Reproduce the failure once (note the exact screen).</li>
            <li>Pull the truth from logcat (next section).</li>
            <li>Apply the fix matrix in order — stop at the first green install.</li>
          </ol>

          <h2>The log never lies</h2>
          <blockquote>
            <p>"If the toast says nothing, <code>adb logcat</code> says everything. Read the install lines before you download a fourth copy of the same APK."</p>
            <cite>— G-will, after fixing the same Tecno Spark issue twice in one week.</cite>
          </blockquote>
          <p>Pull the failure signature:</p>
          <pre><code class="language-bash">adb logcat -c && adb install app-release.apk
adb logcat -d | grep -i "packageinstaller\|install_failed" | tail -n 20</code></pre>
          <div class="tbl-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Log line contains</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE</code></td><td>Old copy signed with a different key</td><td class="tbl-best"><code>adb uninstall -k</code> then reinstall</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>INSTALL_FAILED_INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE</code></td><td>No room (needs ~2× APK)</td><td class="tbl-yes">Free space, clear cache</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES</code></td><td>Corrupt/incomplete download</td><td class="tbl-no">Re-download, check SHA-256</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>INSTALL_FAILED_TEST_ONLY</code></td><td>Debug APK flagged test-only</td><td><code>adb install -t</code> or use release build</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          </div>
          <p>Inline code for the road: run <code>adb shell pm list packages | grep example</code> to confirm the ghost copy is really gone.</p>
          <pre class="verse">The toast says nothing.
The log says everything.
Read it first.</pre>

          <h2>Screenshots</h2>
          <figure>
            <img src="/img/kb-toast.svg" width="800" height="450" alt="Install error toast on Galaxy A14" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption>The famous useless toast. The answer is in logcat, not here.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <p>Gallery (before → after):</p>
          <div class="gallery">
            <figure>
              <img src="/img/kb-storage.svg" width="800" height="450" alt="Storage screen" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption>Settings → Storage: free 2× the APK.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <img src="/img/kb-unknown.svg" width="800" height="450" alt="Unknown sources prompt" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption>Install unknown apps: allow only your file manager.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <img src="/img/kb-success.svg" width="800" height="450" alt="Success screen" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption>Green install. Done.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <h2 id="the-3-minute-fix">The 3-minute fix</h2>
          <figure class="pullquote">
            <blockquote><p>Uninstall the signature conflict first. Everything else is guessing.</p></blockquote>
          </figure>
          <div class="callout warn" role="alert">
            <p><strong>Warning:</strong> <code>adb uninstall</code> WITHOUT <code>-k</code> wipes app data. Keep the <code>-k</code> flag if chats, logins, or game saves matter.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="callout note" role="note">
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Play Protect re-enable after testing. Leaving it off for "faster installs" is how spyware earns a living.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq">
            <details>
              <summary>Play Protect blocked it — now what?</summary>
              <p>Turn it back on after the test install. A blocked sideload that installs fine with Protect off is untrusted until proven otherwise — verify the SHA on the source site.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Are split APKs (.apks) broken?</summary>
              <p>No — they're multi-file by design. Install with Split APK Installer or <code>adb install-multiple base.apk config.arm64.apk</code>.</p>
            </details>
          </div>

          <h2>Buttons, breaks, and motion</h2>
          <p>Grab the tools once, reuse forever:</p>
          <p class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn" href="https://developer.android.com/tools/releases/platform-tools">Download Platform-Tools</a>
            <a class="btn-ghost" href="#the-3-minute-fix">Check SHA-256</a>
            <a class="btn-ghost" href="#the-3-minute-fix">Split APK Installer</a>
          </p>
          <hr />
          <div class="cols">
            <div><h3>Column one</h3><p>Columns stack on phones (≤767px). Two tools side by side on desktop, one column in the hand.</p></div>
            <div><h3>Column two</h3><p>Same reading measure, no squeeze. Covers and groups behave like cards, never like desktop print.</p></div>
          </div>
